Evaluate \(Z = x + 2y\) at each of the four corner points of the feasible region \(PQRS\):
at \(P\left(\frac{3}{13}, \frac{24}{13}\right)\), \(Z = \frac{3}{13} + \frac{48}{13} = \frac{51}{13} \approx 3\cdot92\);
at \(Q\left(\frac{3}{2}, \frac{15}{4}\right)\), \(Z = \frac{3}{2} + \frac{15}{2} = 9\);
at \(R\left(\frac{7}{2}, \frac{3}{4}\right)\), \(Z = \frac{7}{2} + \frac{3}{2} = 5\);
at \(S\left(\frac{18}{7}, \frac{2}{7}\right)\), \(Z = \frac{18}{7} + \frac{4}{7} = \frac{22}{7} \approx 3\cdot14\).
The smallest value is \(\frac{22}{7}\), attained at \(S\), so the correct statement is that Z is minimum at \(S\left(\frac{18}{7}, \frac{2}{7}\right)\). Each of the other three is false: the maximum is \(9\) at \(Q\), not at \(R\); the value at \(P\) is \(\frac{51}{13} \approx 3\cdot92\), which is less than the value \(9\) at \(Q\); and the value at \(Q\) is \(9\), which is greater than the value \(5\) at \(R\).
